     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 queue mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another regimen**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's intentional. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
